l","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wind Drake","oracle_id":"d6ffdaf0-ac08-4de9-bbce-2eab2f86bcca","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-09-30","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Drake"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Icefall Regent’s last ability affects all spells cast by your opponents that target it, including Aura spells and spells with multiple targets. It doesn’t affect abilities.","oracle_id":"0cf18002-1bbe-40b3-ae15-fa51e61e9391","published_at":"2015-02-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Icefall Regent’s triggered ability can target any creature controlled by an opponent, including one that is already tapped. In that case, the creature stays tapped and won’t untap during its controller’s untap step.","oracle_id":"0cf18002-1bbe-40b3-ae15-fa51e61e9391","published_at":"2015-02-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another player gains control of Icefall Regent, the creature will no longer be affected by the ability stopping it from untapping, even if you later regain control of Icefall Regent.","oracle_id":"0cf18002-1bbe-40b3-ae15-fa51e61e9391","published_at":"2015-02-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability stopping the creature from untapping will continue to apply to it even if the creature changes controllers.","oracle_id":"0cf18002-1bbe-40b3-ae15-fa51e61e9391","published_at":"2015-02-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability can target a tapped creature. If the targeted creature is already tapped when it resolves, that creature just remains tapped and doesn’t untap during its controller’s next untap step.","oracle_id":"ab5ebae2-cd77-4a7d-a93b-8042cd486429","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dungeon Geists’s triggered ability can target a tapped creature. If the targeted creature is already tapped when it resolves, that creature just remains tapped and won’t untap during its controller’s untap step.","oracle_id":"ab5ebae2-cd77-4a7d-a93b-8042cd486429","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Dungeon Geists leaves the battlefield before its triggered ability has resolved, the target creature will be tapped, but it will be able to untap as normal.","oracle_id":"ab5ebae2-cd77-4a7d-a93b-8042cd486429","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another player gains control of Dungeon Geists, its effect expires. It won’t keep the creature from untapping anymore, even if you later regain control of Dungeon Geists.","oracle_id":"ab5ebae2-cd77-4a7d-a93b-8042cd486429","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"cd0d7141-46d2-4aa3-bc77-6b3b4513803e","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another player gains control of Tidebinder Mage, the creature will no longer be affected by the ability preventing it from untapping, even if you later regain control of Tidebinder Mage.","oracle_id":"f881378b-b539-4ea8-981d-e01ee82af105","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you gain control of the creature that’s being prevented from untapping, that creature won’t untap during your untap step for as long as you control Tidebinder Mage.","oracle_id":"f881378b-b539-4ea8-981d-e01ee82af105","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you lose control of Tidebinder Mage between when it entered the battlefield and when the ability resolves, the target creature will become tapped. However, it won’t be affected by the other effect and will untap as normal during its controller’s untap step.","oracle_id":"f881378b-b539-4ea8-981d-e01ee82af105","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability can target a tapped creature. If the targeted creature is already tapped when it resolves, that creature just remains tapped and doesn’t untap during its controller’s next untap step.","oracle_id":"f881378b-b539-4ea8-981d-e01ee82af105","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
